WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.920
Model output should be treated as untrusted until it is validated for the destination.

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:15.780
A response may be fluent, confident, and useful while still being incomplete, incorrect, unauthorized, unsafe to render, or inappropriate for an automated workflow.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:27.120
If output will be displayed in HTML, stored in a database, sent to another system, used as JSON, inserted into a ticket, or passed to a tool, it needs the controls appropriate to that destination.

00:00:27.340 --> 00:00:31.580
Structured output validation helps when the application expects fields rather than prose.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:40.840
JSON schema concepts, type checks, allowed values, length limits, and business-rule validation can catch output that does not match the contract.

00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:50.180
Safe rendering and output encoding protect user interfaces when model text includes characters that have special meaning in HTML, Markdown, URLs, or other formats.

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:54.320
Validation and encoding solve different problems, so both may be needed.

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:57.580
Hallucination and uncertainty are security-relevant.

00:00:57.800 --> 00:01:06.600
Incorrect references, invented citations, wrong policy summaries, false confidence, or misleading recommendations can affect user decisions.

00:01:06.820 --> 00:01:16.420
AI applications should ground answers in evidence where possible, show citations when useful, communicate uncertainty, and avoid presenting generated text as verified truth.

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:23.360
For high-impact workflows, the application should require human review or independent verification before decisions are accepted.

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:26.220
User experience is part of the control model.

00:01:26.440 --> 00:01:37.960
Users should understand when they are interacting with an AI system, what data sources may have influenced an answer, what limitations apply, and when a human or authoritative system should be consulted.

00:01:38.180 --> 00:01:41.060
Good UX does not bury safety in long disclaimers.

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:51.200
It gives users practical signals: source references, confidence boundaries, confirmation prompts, warnings before sensitive actions, and clear escalation paths.
